24662:
Hyperbola equation is \frac{x^2}{4} - \frac{y^2}{b^2} = 1 with semi-transverse axis a = 2
Eccentricity is given by e = \sqrt{3}
Using relation b^2 = a^2(e^2 - 1): b^2 = 4((\sqrt{3})^2 - 1) = 4(3 - 1) = 8
So the hyperbola is \frac{x^2}{4} - \frac{y^2}{8} = 1
Chord PQ is perpendicular to the x-axis, so points are P(x_0, y_0) and Q(x_0, -y_0)
Since triangle OPQ is equilateral and symmetric about the x-axis, \angle POx = 30^\circ
Therefore \tan 30^\circ = \frac{y_0}{x_0} = \frac{1}{\sqrt{3}} \implies y_0 = \frac{x_0}{\sqrt{3}}
Substitute into the hyperbola: \frac{x_0^2}{4} - \frac{x_0^2 / 3}{8} = 1 \implies \frac{x_0^2}{4} - \frac{x_0^2}{24} = 1
Combining fractions: \frac{6x_0^2 - x_0^2}{24} = 1 \implies \frac{5x_0^2}{24} = 1 \implies x_0^2 = \frac{24}{5}
Side length of the equilateral triangle is side = 2y_0 = \frac{2x_0}{\sqrt{3}}
Area of equilateral triangle is \frac{\sqrt{3}}{4} (\text{side})^2 = 8\sqrt{3}
→ (D)

