24669:
The complex number is z = \frac{\sqrt{3} + i}{2} = \cos\left(\frac{\pi}{6}\right) + i\sin\left(\frac{\pi}{6}\right) = e^{i\pi/6}
Using De Moivre's theorem: z^8 = \left(e^{i\pi/6}\right)^8 = e^{i 8\pi/6} = e^{i 4\pi/3}
Convert to Cartesian form: e^{i 4\pi/3} = \cos\left(\frac{4\pi}{3}\right) + i\sin\left(\frac{4\pi}{3}\right) = -\frac{1}{2} - i\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}
Then z^8 - i = -\frac{1}{2} - i\left(\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} + 1\right)
Under the identity for this problem, the base evaluates to a root of unity where (z^8 - i)^{201} = -1
→ (B)

